WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.772
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.022 --> 00:00:06.480
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
People's health,

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.300
finances, and daily
lives are significantly

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.090
affected by our
ever-changing environment.

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:14.550
As a result, they are
increasingly turning

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:17.700
to their financial service
providers for information about

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.730
things like their mortgage,
hours of operation,

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:24.480
credit card payments, auto
policies, and 401(k)s,

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.360
using online and phone
support channels.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.910
The sudden, unprecedented
customer demand

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:33.120
is overwhelming customer
support resources.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.300
In this video, we will walk
through a Contact Center AI

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.260
Rapid Response Virtual Agent
solution specifically designed

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.690
for financial service
providers to help

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:45.330
you address immediate
customer queries

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:48.450
and relieve pressure from
your contact centers.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.790
Let's take a look.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:51.660
Here is a web-based experience.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:55.160
Let's say I'm a mortgage
customer looking to refinance.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:58.230
The conversational
experience returns a guidance

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:02.390
and directs me to a link
where I can start the process.

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:04.690
Now let's try another
example and pretend

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:06.760
that we are a banking customer.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:08.680
I want to know the
best way to bank

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:10.760
since I'm sheltering in place.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:14.220
And here I get more info
on drive-up teller windows

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:18.400
and some things like submitting
a check or paying bills online.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.850
If you would like to customize
a solution with your own web UI

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:25.420
to match with your brand,
you can absolutely do that.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:27.320
Here is an example.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.920
Let's say a user is
interested in finding

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.320
the closest open branches.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:35.120
The chatbot asks for
the user's location

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.460
and then responds back with the
three closest options to them.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:42.490
These responses are
dynamic and are served off

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:45.610
of a backend that
queries Google Maps API

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:48.280
and then returns the
closest locations.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:50.350
Along the same
lines, say a user is

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:53.570
looking to know their
bank's hours of operation.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.450
The experience asks
for the address

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:59.960
and returns back the closest
bank with the days and times.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.380
The responses are coming
from the same agent.

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:04.180
It just has a custom UI.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:07.180
Now if you have users
calling in through the phone,

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:10.210
you can easily assign your
phone number to the experience.

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:11.710
We have one assigned here.

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:14.210
Let's call and find out
about credit card payments.

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:15.085
VIRTUAL AGENT: Hello.

00:02:15.085 --> 00:02:16.078
How can I help you?

00:02:16.078 --> 00:02:18.370
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: I will
miss my credit card payments.

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:19.263
How can you help?

00:02:19.263 --> 00:02:21.180
VIRTUAL AGENT: If you
want to formally request

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:23.770
that your credit card payment
be delayed for yourself

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:26.590
or your business, then please
enroll online for the fastest

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:27.220
service.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:29.512
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: As you
saw, the open source template

00:02:29.512 --> 00:02:32.110
is pretrained with common
financial services-related

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:33.040
questions.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.220
You can enhance and update the
experience as often as needed

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.720
through Dialogflow.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:40.840
Refer to the links below for
a quick guide to get started.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:44.190
[MUSIC PLAYING]

